{"task_id": "Mbpp/4", "solution": "import heapq\n\ndef _validate_inputs(numbers, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates input parameters according to business rules.\n    It checks if n is non-negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    return n >= 0\n\ndef _build_max_heap(numbers):\n    \"\"\"\n    Creates a min-heap of negative numbers to simulate a max-heap.\n    This allows `heappop` to extract the largest original numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_heap_sim = [-x for x in numbers]\n    heapq.heapify(max_heap_sim)\n    return max_heap_sim\n\ndef _extract_n_largest(heap, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts n largest elements from the simulated max-heap.\n    Elements are negated back to their original positive values during extraction.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    # Determine the actual number of elements to extract, limited by the heap size.\n    num_to_extract = min(n, len(heap))\n    for _ in range(num_to_extract):\n        # heappop retrieves the smallest item (most negative) from the min-heap,\n        # which corresponds to the largest original number (least negative).\n        result.append(-heapq.heappop(heap))\n    return result\n\ndef _sort_descending(result):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts the result list in descending order.\n    Elements extracted from the simulated max-heap are already in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    return result\n\ndef heap_queue_largest(numbers, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the n largest integers from a given list of numbers, returned in descending order.\n    It uses a heap-based algorithm for efficient selection.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle initial edge cases: invalid n, n=0, or an empty input list.\n    if not _validate_inputs(numbers, n) or n == 0 or not numbers:\n        return []\n\n    # Build a min-heap of negated numbers to simulate a max-heap.\n    max_heap_simulated = _build_max_heap(numbers)\n\n    # Extract the n largest elements from the simulated max-heap.\n    largest_elements = _extract_n_largest(max_heap_simulated, n)\n\n    # Sort the extracted elements in descending order (they are already in this order).\n    final_result = _sort_descending(largest_elements)\n\n    return final_result"}
