{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "def sort_matrix(matrix: List[List[Union[int, float]]]) -> List[List[Union[int, float]]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sort matrix rows in ascending order according to their sum.\n    Returns a new matrix with rows sorted by sum, maintaining relative order for equal sums.\n    \"\"\"\n    rows_with_sums = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        rows_with_sums.append((sum(row), row))\n\n    # Python's sorted() is stable, which preserves the original order for rows with equal sums.\n    sorted_rows_with_sums = sorted(rows_with_sums, key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    # Extract just the original rows from the sorted (sum, row) tuples.\n    result_matrix = [row for _, row in sorted_rows_with_sums]\n\n    return result_matrix"}
