{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "def check(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    Uses a helper function to reverse the digits of the number.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _reverse_number(n):\n        \"\"\"Reverses the digits of an integer.\"\"\"\n        reversed_n = 0\n        while n > 0:\n            digit = n % 10\n            reversed_n = reversed_n * 10 + digit\n            n //= 10\n        return reversed_n\n\n    reversed_num = _reverse_number(number)\n    return number == (2 * reversed_num) - 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/20", "solution": "def is_woodall(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if the given number is a Woodall number.\n    A Woodall number follows the formula n \u00d7 2^n - 1 for some positive integer n.\n    \"\"\"\n    def calculate_woodall(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculate Woodall number using formula n \u00d7 2^n - 1.\"\"\"\n        return n * (2**n) - 1\n\n    if number <= 0:\n        return False\n\n    n = 1\n    while True:\n        woodall_candidate = calculate_woodall(n)\n        if woodall_candidate == number:\n            return True\n        elif woodall_candidate > number:\n            return False\n        n += 1"}
