{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "def is_sublist(main_list: list, sublist: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check if sublist appears as contiguous sequence in main_list.\"\"\"\n    if not sublist:\n        return True\n    if not main_list:\n        return False\n\n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sublist)\n\n    if m > n:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        # Check if the slice of main_list matches the sublist\n        match = True\n        for j in range(m):\n            if main_list[i + j] != sublist[j]:\n                match = False\n                break\n        if match:\n            return True\n            \n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "def is_sublist(main_list, sublist):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a sublist is present as a contiguous sequence within a main list.\n    Handles empty list edge cases efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    len_main = len(main_list)\n    len_sub = len(sublist)\n\n    # Handle empty sublist: an empty list is always a sublist\n    if len_sub == 0:\n        return True\n    \n    # Handle case where sublist is longer than main list or main list is empty\n    if len_main < len_sub or len_main == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Iterate through the main list to find a potential starting point\n    for i in range(len_main - len_sub + 1):\n        # Compare the slice of main_list with the sublist\n        if main_list[i : i + len_sub] == sublist:\n            return True\n\n    return False"}
