{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "def comb_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of elements in ascending order using the comb sort algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    \n    # Initialize gap to the size of the array\n    gap = n\n    \n    # Flag to track if any swaps were made in the current pass\n    swapped = True\n    \n    SHRINK_FACTOR = 1.3 # The shrink factor used in comb sort.\n\n    def _calculate_gap(current_gap: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the next gap value for the comb sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n        new_gap = int(current_gap / SHRINK_FACTOR)\n        return max(1, new_gap)\n\n    def _swap(elements: list, i: int, j: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Swaps two elements in a list at the specified indices.\"\"\"\n        elements[i], elements[j] = elements[j], elements[i]\n\n    # Continue sorting until gap is 1 and no swaps are made in the last pass\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        # Update the gap value for the current pass\n        gap = _calculate_gap(gap)\n        \n        swapped = False # Reset swapped flag for the current pass\n        \n        # Perform a single pass with the current gap\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr[i] > arr[i + gap]:\n                _swap(arr, i, i + gap)\n                swapped = True\n                \n    return arr"}
