{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if a number is undulating (alternates between exactly two different digits).\n    An undulating number must have at least 3 digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n\n    s_number = str(number)\n    if len(s_number) < 3:\n        return False\n\n    digit1 = int(s_number[0])\n    digit2 = int(s_number[1])\n\n    if digit1 == digit2:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(2, len(s_number)):\n        current_digit = int(s_number[i])\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # Even index (0-based) should match digit1\n            if current_digit != digit1:\n                return False\n        else:  # Odd index (0-based) should match digit2\n            if current_digit != digit2:\n                return False\n\n    return True"}
