{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check if number can be represented as sum of distinct non-zero powers of 2.\n    This implies the number must be positive, even, and its binary representation must not have consecutive 1s.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 0:\n        return False\n    \n    # \"Non-zero powers of 2\" implies exponents k >= 1 (excluding 2^0 = 1).\n    # This means the number must be even (its least significant bit must be 0).\n    if number % 2 != 0:\n        return False\n\n    # The design context mentions checking for \"no consecutive 1s in its binary representation\".\n    # This is true if `number` AND `number` right-shifted by 1 is 0.\n    if (number & (number >> 1)) != 0:\n        return False\n\n    return True"}
