{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "def sum_range_list(numbers: list, start_index: int, end_index: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of numbers in a list within a specified range (inclusive).\n    Handles out-of-bounds indices and empty lists gracefully by returning 0 for invalid ranges.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(numbers)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Adjust indices to be within valid list bounds\n    actual_start = max(0, start_index)\n    actual_end = min(n - 1, end_index)\n\n    # If the adjusted range is invalid (start > end), return 0\n    if actual_start > actual_end:\n        return 0\n\n    # Sum the slice from actual_start (inclusive) to actual_end (inclusive)\n    return sum(numbers[actual_start : actual_end + 1])"}
