{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    The majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _find_first_occurrence(arr: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the first occurrence of the target in a sorted array.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        first_idx = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                first_idx = mid\n                high = mid - 1  # Try to find an even earlier occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return first_idx\n\n    def _find_last_occurrence(arr: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of the target in a sorted array.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        last_idx = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                last_idx = mid\n                low = mid + 1  # Try to find an even later occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return last_idx\n\n    # If the array is empty, no element can be a majority.\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    first_index = _find_first_occurrence(array, element)\n\n    # If the element is not found, it cannot be a majority element.\n    if first_index == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_index = _find_last_occurrence(array, element)\n\n    # Calculate the count of the element.\n    count = last_index - first_index + 1\n\n    # Check if the count exceeds n/2.\n    return count > n / 2"}
