{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\n\ndef next_Perfect_Square(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the smallest perfect square greater than the given number.\n    It uses mathematical functions to achieve O(1) time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate the square root of 'number + 1'. This helps find the starting point\n    # for the next integer whose square will be greater than the original number.\n    sqrt_plus_one = math.sqrt(number + 1)\n\n    # Find the smallest integer greater than or equal to sqrt_plus_one.\n    # Squaring this integer will yield the next perfect square.\n    next_root = math.ceil(sqrt_plus_one)\n\n    # Return the square of this integer, ensuring the final result is an integer.\n    return int(next_root * next_root)"}
