{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    Uses dynamic programming to build up solutions for substrings.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromic subsequences of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for lengths from 2 to n\n    # 'length' is the length of the substring (j - i + 1)\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If characters match, they contribute to the palindrome.\n                # Add 2 to the LPS of the inner substring s[i+1...j-1].\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                # If characters do not match, take the maximum of excluding s[i] or s[j].\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
