{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return array[0]\n\n    def _find_increasing_sums(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates maximum increasing subsequence sums ending at each position.\"\"\"\n        inc_sums = list(arr)\n        for i in range(1, n):\n            for j in range(i):\n                if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                    inc_sums[i] = max(inc_sums[i], arr[i] + inc_sums[j])\n        return inc_sums\n\n    def _find_decreasing_sums(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates maximum decreasing subsequence sums starting at each position.\"\"\"\n        dec_sums = list(arr)\n        for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n            for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n                if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                    dec_sums[i] = max(dec_sums[i], arr[i] + dec_sums[j])\n        return dec_sums\n\n    inc_sums = _find_increasing_sums(array)\n    dec_sums = _find_decreasing_sums(array)\n\n    max_bitonic_sum = max(array) # A single element is considered a bitonic subsequence.\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        # The element array[i] is the peak, counted in both increasing and decreasing parts.\n        current_sum = inc_sums[i] + dec_sums[i] - array[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
