{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "def maximize_elements(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compares corresponding tuple pairs from two input tuples element-wise\n    and returns a new tuple containing the maximum values from each position.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for pair1, pair2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        max_first = max(pair1[0], pair2[0])\n        max_second = max(pair1[1], pair2[1])\n        result.append((max_first, max_second))\n    return tuple(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "def maximize_elements(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Maximizes elements of two tuples by comparing corresponding inner tuples element-wise.\n    Returns a new tuple where each inner tuple contains the maximum values from the inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _compare_elements(elem1, elem2):\n        \"\"\"\n        Compares two inner tuples element-wise and returns a new tuple with the maximums.\n        \"\"\"\n        return (max(elem1[0], elem2[0]), max(elem1[1], elem2[1]))\n\n    result = []\n    for pair1, pair2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        result.append(_compare_elements(pair1, pair2))\n    return tuple(result)"}
