{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "def list_split(input_list, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list into n sublists by distributing elements in a round-robin fashion.\n    Each element from the input_list is added to a sublist based on its original index modulo n.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_sublists = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    for index, element in enumerate(input_list):\n        target_sublist_index = index % n\n        result_sublists[target_sublist_index].append(element)\n    \n    return result_sublists"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/267", "solution": "def square_Sum(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of squares of the first n odd natural numbers.\n    For n=2, the odd numbers are 1, 3. Their squares are 1, 9, and the sum is 10.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for k in range(1, n + 1):\n        odd_number = (2 * k) - 1\n        total_sum += odd_number ** 2\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/267", "solution": "def square_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the sum of squares of the first n odd natural numbers.\n    For n=2, first two odd numbers are 1 and 3. Sum of squares is 1*1 + 3*3 = 1 + 9 = 10.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        odd_number = 2 * i + 1\n        total_sum += odd_number * odd_number\n    return total_sum"}
