{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "def validate(integer: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    Handles negative integers by considering their absolute value.\n    \"\"\"\n    abs_integer_str = str(abs(integer))\n    digit_counts = [0] * 10  # counts[i] will store the frequency of digit i\n\n    for char_digit in abs_integer_str:\n        digit = int(char_digit)\n        digit_counts[digit] += 1\n\n    for digit_value in range(10):\n        frequency = digit_counts[digit_value]\n        if frequency > digit_value:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "def validate(integer):\n    # Converts the integer to a string to iterate through its digits.\n    # Counts digit frequencies and checks if each digit's frequency is less than or equal to its value.\n    s_integer = str(integer)\n    \n    # Using a dictionary to store digit frequencies\n    digit_frequencies = {}\n    for char_digit in s_integer:\n        digit_frequencies[char_digit] = digit_frequencies.get(char_digit, 0) + 1\n        \n    for char_digit, frequency in digit_frequencies.items():\n        digit_value = int(char_digit)\n        if frequency > digit_value:\n            return False\n            \n    return True"}
