{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(array, array_length, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in a modified array formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _kadane(arr):\n        \"\"\"Applies Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum sum of a contiguous subarray in a single array.\"\"\"\n        if not arr:\n            return 0\n        max_so_far = arr[0]\n        current_max = arr[0]\n        for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n            current_max = max(arr[i], current_max + arr[i])\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n        return max_so_far\n\n    # Handle edge cases: empty conceptual array (k=0) or empty input array\n    if k == 0 or array_length == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate max sum for a single instance of the array\n    max_kadane_single = _kadane(array)\n\n    # If k is 1, the result is simply Kadane's on the single array\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_kadane_single\n\n    # Calculate total sum of the original array\n    total_array_sum = sum(array)\n\n    # Calculate max prefix sum of a contiguous subarray (must include at least one element)\n    max_prefix_sum_val = -float('inf')\n    current_prefix_sum = 0\n    for x in array:\n        current_prefix_sum += x\n        max_prefix_sum_val = max(max_prefix_sum_val, current_prefix_sum)\n    \n    # Calculate max suffix sum of a contiguous subarray (must include at least one element)\n    max_suffix_sum_val = -float('inf')\n    current_suffix_sum = 0\n    for x in reversed(array):\n        current_suffix_sum += x\n        max_suffix_sum_val = max(max_suffix_sum_val, current_suffix_sum)\n\n    # Initialize the overall maximum with the max sum from a single array\n    max_overall = max_kadane_single\n\n    # Case for k >= 2: The sum could span across two arrays (suffix of first + prefix of second)\n    # This covers subarrays that cross the array boundary exactly once.\n    max_overall = max(max_overall, max_prefix_sum_val + max_suffix_sum_val)\n\n    # Case for k > 2 and total_array_sum is positive:\n    # If the total sum of the array is positive, repeating full arrays between a max prefix and max suffix\n    # can further increase the sum.\n    if total_array_sum > 0 and k > 2:\n        max_overall = max(max_overall, max_prefix_sum_val + (k - 2) * total_array_sum + max_suffix_sum_val)\n    \n    # If total_array_sum is negative or zero, adding more full arrays (k-2) won't help or will reduce\n    # the sum, so the previous calculations (single array max, or two-array span) are sufficient.\n\n    return max_overall"}
