{"task_id": "Mbpp/294", "solution": "class NoNumericValuesError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception raised when no numeric values are found in the list.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message=\"No numeric values found in the list.\"):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\ndef _is_numeric(value):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a value is a numeric type (int or float).\"\"\"\n    return isinstance(value, (int, float))\n\ndef _filter_numeric_values(input_list):\n    \"\"\"Filters a list, returning only numeric values.\"\"\"\n    return [item for item in input_list if _is_numeric(item)]\n\ndef max_val(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum numeric value in a given heterogeneous list.\n    Non-numeric elements are ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    numeric_values = _filter_numeric_values(input_list)\n\n    if not numeric_values:\n        raise NoNumericValuesError(\"No numeric values found in the list.\")\n\n    return max(numeric_values)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "def get_Inv_Count(arr: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of inversions in an array.\n    An inversion occurs when arr[i] > arr[j] and i < j.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    inv_count = 0\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                inv_count += 1\n    return inv_count"}
