{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(array: list[int], length: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from array[0...i] that includes array[k].\n    The subsequence must end with an element from array[0...i] that is less than array[k].\n    \"\"\"\n    # The value at index k must be included in the subsequence.\n    k_value = array[k]\n\n    # dp[x] will store the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at index x.\n    # Initialize dp with array[x], as each element itself is an increasing subsequence of sum array[x].\n    dp = list(array) \n\n    # max_prefix_sum stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence\n    # ending at an index j <= i, such that array[j] < k_value.\n    max_prefix_sum = 0\n\n    # Iterate through the prefix of the array up to index i (inclusive).\n    for x in range(i + 1):\n        # For each element array[x], find previous elements array[y] (y < x)\n        # that can extend an increasing subsequence.\n        for y in range(x):\n            if array[x] > array[y]:\n                dp[x] = max(dp[x], dp[y] + array[x])\n        \n        # After calculating dp[x], if array[x] can precede k_value in an increasing subsequence,\n        # update max_prefix_sum.\n        if array[x] < k_value:\n            max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, dp[x])\n            \n    # The total maximum sum is the max_prefix_sum (from 0 to i, less than k_value)\n    # plus the mandatory k_value itself.\n    # If no element in array[0...i] is smaller than k_value, max_prefix_sum will be 0,\n    # and the result will just be k_value (meaning the subsequence is only array[k]).\n    return max_prefix_sum + k_value"}
