{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(array, length, i, k):\n    # dp[j] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence\n    # ending at array[j] from the prefix array[0...j].\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n\n    # Calculate dp values for the prefix array[0...i].\n    # Each dp[j] is initialized with array[j] itself, as it forms an IS of sum array[j].\n    # Then, it checks if array[j] can extend any previous increasing subsequence.\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        dp[j] = array[j]\n        for prev in range(j):\n            if array[j] > array[prev]:\n                dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[prev] + array[j])\n\n    # Find the maximum sum from dp[0...i] such that\n    # the corresponding element array[j] is less than array[k].\n    # This ensures array[k] can extend the chosen subsequence.\n    max_prefix_subsequence_sum = 0\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if array[j] < array[k]:\n            max_prefix_subsequence_sum = max(max_prefix_subsequence_sum, dp[j])\n\n    # The total maximum sum is the best prefix sum found (which can be 0 if no\n    # suitable prefix element exists) plus the mandatory element at array[k].\n    return max_prefix_subsequence_sum + array[k]"}
