{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "def first_non_repeating_character(input_string: str) -> str | None:\n    # Counts the frequency of each character in the given string.\n    def _count_character_frequency(s: str) -> dict[str, int]:\n        frequency_map = {}\n        for char in s:\n            frequency_map[char] = frequency_map.get(char, 0) + 1\n        return frequency_map\n\n    # Finds the first character in the string that has a frequency of 1.\n    def _find_first_unique(s: str, frequency_map: dict[str, int]) -> str | None:\n        for char in s:\n            if frequency_map[char] == 1:\n                return char\n        return None\n\n    if not input_string:\n        return None\n\n    frequency_map = _count_character_frequency(input_string)\n    return _find_first_unique(input_string, frequency_map)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/397", "solution": "def median_numbers(num1, num2, num3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median of three numbers, returning the result as a float.\n    It identifies the middle value after sorting and converts it to a float.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def sort_three_numbers(a, b, c):\n        \"\"\"Sorts three numbers in ascending order and returns them as a tuple.\"\"\"\n        numbers_list = [a, b, c]\n        numbers_list.sort()\n        return tuple(numbers_list)\n\n    def convert_to_float(value):\n        \"\"\"Converts a numeric value to a float type.\"\"\"\n        return float(value)\n\n    # Use the defined helper to sort the numbers\n    sorted_numbers = sort_three_numbers(num1, num2, num3)\n\n    # The median is the middle element (index 1) of the sorted tuple\n    middle_value = sorted_numbers[1]\n\n    # Use the defined helper to convert the median to a float\n    return convert_to_float(middle_value)"}
